{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CmwwUkFd3HET75E93KfdiE","type":"tool_result","content":"     556 test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc\n    1898 test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc\n     963 src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc\n    3417 total\nanalysis_test.cljc\ncode_test.cljc\ncorpus.cljc\nderive_test.cljc\neffects_test.cljc\nframe_test.cljc\nlayout_test.cljc\nlinearize_test.cljc\nlink_test.cljc\nload_paths_test.cljc\nparity_test.cljc\nsafepoint_harness_test.cljc\nscan_test.cljc\nscanner_goldens.cljc\nvm_test.cljc\nwalker_trace_test.cljc\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-13 +07\n# Slice 6c fix round 1 (engineer report, opus)\n\nBranch `srvm-phase6c`, worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c`. HEAD is still 47ddb1d9. **Not committed.**\n\nThis round implements work-list items 1 to 7 of `collab/1792360000000-architect-6c-rulings.report.md`, in order.\n\n## Scope\n\nI did not edit any design doc, kernel, `rows.cljc`, `semantic_register.cljc` or `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/*`. `git diff --quiet -- docs src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc` is clean.\n\n| File | +/- |\n|---|---|\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc` | +~80 / -7 |\n| `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc` | +~145 / -10 |\n| `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` | +~360 / -70 |\n| `test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj` | +13 / -1 |\n\n## Item 1: F6 and the store-write audit\n\n**Change.**\n- Removed the unused `[yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]` require from `layout_test.cljc`.\n- Added `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc {[\"canonical-task\" \"assoc\"] 1, [\"kernel-task\" \"assoc\"] 1}` to the audit allowlist. The reason written beside it is the ruling's: state construction over keys that already passed the one program-write gate, with the `restore-task` and `isolated-receiver` precedent. These writes are not routed through `store-put`.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n- `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test`: 3 tests, 129 assertions, 0 failures.\n- Kondo: `clj -M:kondo --lint` on all four touched files gives **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n  - `clojure -M:kondo` was refused by this session's permission gate.\n  - `clj -M:kondo` (the same alias) ran.\n\n## Item 2: R3, free-environment values\n\n**Change (`layout.cljc`).**\n- **Lower:** `lower-defect` has a new clause that applies to both de Bruijn kinds. It fires on a `:closure` or `:reified` row in the carried `free-env` slot (slot 5), or one reached through guest collections in it. It refuses `:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value {:yin.k/path [:free-env sym …]}`. The helpers are `row-procedure` and `free-env-procedure`.\n- **Lift:** `canonical-task` refuses `:yin.k/non-portable :free-env-value {:yin.k/key sym}` when the kernel's `:free-env` is or holds a closure or continuation (`holds-procedure?`). The check runs right after the `:installs` check, so before `rows/lift-task`, which is the only server.\n- Primitives, data and cursor references are still admitted and copied as before.\n\n**Test: `layout-test/free-env-values`.** The fixture is codex's probe 2 (`free-closure-world`): an identity closure `f` made on the world's own lane, placed in `:free-env`, and the program `(then (next-of c) (f \"B\"))`.\n- On the reference lane, both the reference run and `handed-off` answer `\"B\"`. The carrier still admits the value.\n- `lane-lower` into `:stack` and `:register` refuses `[:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value]` with path `[:free-env f]` and zero attaches.\n- A world built on `:stack` or `:register` refuses at lift with `:non-portable :free-env-value`, key `f`, and zero serves.\n\n**Fails before the fix.** Against HEAD's `layout.cljc` the test gives 10 failures out of 21 assertions.\n\n## Item 3: R1, collision preflight and harness scoping\n\n**Change (`layout.cljc`).** `lower-defect` now opens with the `image-collision` clause. It derives the receiver kind's image identity for every carried A: `:stack` uses `dcode/image-hash` of `derive/stack-image`, `:register` uses `rcode/register-hash` of `derive/register-image`. When two A share one identity it refuses:\n\n```\n:yin.k/unsupported :ambiguous-image {:yin.k/image ident :yin.k/segments #{A …}}\n```\n\nThe lift side is unchanged: `canonical-task` raises `:non-portable :ambiguous-image` through `image-segment` before `rows/lift-task` serves anything.\n\n**Change (harness).**\n- New dynamic var `*projected*` and helper `scoped`.\n- `project` also records into `*projected*` when it is bound.\n- `kernel-space` reads `*projected*` when it is bound, and the global `code-index` otherwise.\n- `lane-root` (law 4) and `crossed` (law 5) now run inside `scoped`.\n\n**Test: `layout-test/alpha-equivalent-segments`.**\n- `(fn [x] x)` and `(fn [y] y)` have distinct `:address` and equal `:register-id` and `:stack-id`.\n- **Lift refusal.** A reader parked inside `((fn [x] (then :alpha (next-of c))) 0)`, built on each native lane, is lifted with `layout/space` of the x and y vectors. It refuses `:non-portable :ambiguous-image` with zero serves.\n- **Harness scoping, on both lanes.** With the file-wide index, `lane-lift` also refuses. Inside `scoped`, `kernel-space` holds only the x vector and the lift succeeds.\n- **Lower refusal.** A reference-lane task with both alpha-equivalent closures as store values is lowered into each native lane. It refuses `:unsupported :ambiguous-image`, names both A in `:yin.k/segments`, and makes zero attaches.\n- **Survivor.** The same task lowered into the reference lane passes `h/laws` (laws 1, 2, 3 and 6) and answers `\"B\"`.\n- The fixtures use test-unique shapes (a `:alpha` literal). That way the globally recorded y vector cannot widen another test's unscoped `kernel-space`, for example layout-test's `:closure-value` `(fn [x] x)`.\n\n**Fails before the fix.** I applied two mutants together: the collision clause disabled, and `kernel-space` ignoring `*projected*`. The test then gives 8 failures and 2 errors. The scoping assertions failed (line 492) and the lower refusal assertions failed (lines 504-506).\n\n## Item 4: R4, law-4 controls\n\n**Change (harness).**\n- **Injectivity.** `logical-names` and `ring-names` assert it through `injective`.\n- **`task-root`** is the old `logical-root` body over a decoded task. It also asserts that no lane identity survives in the canonical rows: neither the served ids nor the ring identities.\n- **`lane-root`** now returns `{:root :reference :lane :descriptors :task :machine :peer}`.\n- **`canonical-equality`** asserts:\n  - `(= 3 (count roots))`;\n  - `(= [:semantic-register :stack :register] (mapv :lane roots))`;\n  - one root;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1571a1be-fcf5-41b6-a2c4-f2a5582b2e60","uuid":"b879900e-3ff0-418d-bb27-db7b15a2263c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:03:57.010Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     556 test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc\n    1898 test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc\n     963 src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc\n    3417 total\nanalysis_test.cljc\ncode_test.cljc\ncorpus.cljc\nderive_test.cljc\neffects_test.cljc\nframe_test.cljc\nlayout_test.cljc\nlinearize_test.cljc\nlink_test.cljc\nload_paths_test.cljc\nparity_test.cljc\nsafepoint_harness_test.cljc\nscan_test.cljc\nscanner_goldens.cljc\nvm_test.cljc\nwalker_trace_test.cljc\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-13 +07\n# Slice 6c fix round 1 (engineer report, opus)\n\nBranch `srvm-phase6c`, worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c`. HEAD is still 47ddb1d9. **Not committed.**\n\nThis round implements work-list items 1 to 7 of `collab/1792360000000-architect-6c-rulings.report.md`, in order.\n\n## Scope\n\nI did not edit any design doc, kernel, `rows.cljc`, `semantic_register.cljc` or `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/*`. `git diff --quiet -- docs src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc` is clean.\n\n| File | +/- |\n|---|---|\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc` | +~80 / -7 |\n| `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc` | +~145 / -10 |\n| `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` | +~360 / -70 |\n| `test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj` | +13 / -1 |\n\n## Item 1: F6 and the store-write audit\n\n**Change.**\n- Removed the unused `[yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]` require from `layout_test.cljc`.\n- Added `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc {[\"canonical-task\" \"assoc\"] 1, [\"kernel-task\" \"assoc\"] 1}` to the audit allowlist. The reason written beside it is the ruling's: state construction over keys that already passed the one program-write gate, with the `restore-task` and `isolated-receiver` precedent. These writes are not routed through `store-put`.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n- `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test`: 3 tests, 129 assertions, 0 failures.\n- Kondo: `clj -M:kondo --lint` on all four touched files gives **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n  - `clojure -M:kondo` was refused by this session's permission gate.\n  - `clj -M:kondo` (the same alias) ran.\n\n## Item 2: R3, free-environment values\n\n**Change (`layout.cljc`).**\n- **Lower:** `lower-defect` has a new clause that applies to both de Bruijn kinds. It fires on a `:closure` or `:reified` row in the carried `free-env` slot (slot 5), or one reached through guest collections in it. It refuses `:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value {:yin.k/path [:free-env sym …]}`. The helpers are `row-procedure` and `free-env-procedure`.\n- **Lift:** `canonical-task` refuses `:yin.k/non-portable :free-env-value {:yin.k/key sym}` when the kernel's `:free-env` is or holds a closure or continuation (`holds-procedure?`). The check runs right after the `:installs` check, so before `rows/lift-task`, which is the only server.\n- Primitives, data and cursor references are still admitted and copied as before.\n\n**Test: `layout-test/free-env-values`.** The fixture is codex's probe 2 (`free-closure-world`): an identity closure `f` made on the world's own lane, placed in `:free-env`, and the program `(then (next-of c) (f \"B\"))`.\n- On the reference lane, both the reference run and `handed-off` answer `\"B\"`. The carrier still admits the value.\n- `lane-lower` into `:stack` and `:register` refuses `[:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value]` with path `[:free-env f]` and zero attaches.\n- A world built on `:stack` or `:register` refuses at lift with `:non-portable :free-env-value`, key `f`, and zero serves.\n\n**Fails before the fix.** Against HEAD's `layout.cljc` the test gives 10 failures out of 21 assertions.\n\n## Item 3: R1, collision preflight and harness scoping\n\n**Change (`layout.cljc`).** `lower-defect` now opens with the `image-collision` clause. It derives the receiver kind's image identity for every carried A: `:stack` uses `dcode/image-hash` of `derive/stack-image`, `:register` uses `rcode/register-hash` of `derive/register-image`. When two A share one identity it refuses:\n\n```\n:yin.k/unsupported :ambiguous-image {:yin.k/image ident :yin.k/segments #{A …}}\n```\n\nThe lift side is unchanged: `canonical-task` raises `:non-portable :ambiguous-image` through `image-segment` before `rows/lift-task` serves anything.\n\n**Change (harness).**\n- New dynamic var `*projected*` and helper `scoped`.\n- `project` also records into `*projected*` when it is bound.\n- `kernel-space` reads `*projected*` when it is bound, and the global `code-index` otherwise.\n- `lane-root` (law 4) and `crossed` (law 5) now run inside `scoped`.\n\n**Test: `layout-test/alpha-equivalent-segments`.**\n- `(fn [x] x)` and `(fn [y] y)` have distinct `:address` and equal `:register-id` and `:stack-id`.\n- **Lift refusal.** A reader parked inside `((fn [x] (then :alpha (next-of c))) 0)`, built on each native lane, is lifted with `layout/space` of the x and y vectors. It refuses `:non-portable :ambiguous-image` with zero serves.\n- **Harness scoping, on both lanes.** With the file-wide index, `lane-lift` also refuses. Inside `scoped`, `kernel-space` holds only the x vector and the lift succeeds.\n- **Lower refusal.** A reference-lane task with both alpha-equivalent closures as store values is lowered into each native lane. It refuses `:unsupported :ambiguous-image`, names both A in `:yin.k/segments`, and makes zero attaches.\n- **Survivor.** The same task lowered into the reference lane passes `h/laws` (laws 1, 2, 3 and 6) and answers `\"B\"`.\n- The fixtures use test-unique shapes (a `:alpha` literal). That way the globally recorded y vector cannot widen another test's unscoped `kernel-space`, for example layout-test's `:closure-value` `(fn [x] x)`.\n\n**Fails before the fix.** I applied two mutants together: the collision clause disabled, and `kernel-space` ignoring `*projected*`. The test then gives 8 failures and 2 errors. The scoping assertions failed (line 492) and the lower refusal assertions failed (lines 504-506).\n\n## Item 4: R4, law-4 controls\n\n**Change (harness).**\n- **Injectivity.** `logical-names` and `ring-names` assert it through `injective`.\n- **`task-root`** is the old `logical-root` body over a decoded task. It also asserts that no lane identity survives in the canonical rows: neither the served ids nor the ring identities.\n- **`lane-root`** now returns `{:root :reference :lane :descriptors :task :machine :peer}`.\n- **`canonical-equality`** asserts:\n  - `(= 3 (count roots))`;\n  - `(= [:semantic-register :stack :register] (mapv :lane roots))`;\n  - one root;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CmwwUkFd3HET75E93KfdiE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
