{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FW8sD23KRyw7aeQJT4bDq9","type":"tool_result","content":" M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc\nsrc+docs clean","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1571a1be-fcf5-41b6-a2c4-f2a5582b2e60","uuid":"a7c26b0c-fb09-4afe-8027-89de0afe6828","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:17:20.855Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc\nsrc+docs clean","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FW8sD23KRyw7aeQJT4bDq9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxxcQHBTBpH3jheSUuXs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016EKPM4urV31XfrdJBNv8vY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/collab/1792390000000-engineer-6c-fix2.report.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 +07\n# Slice 6c fix round 2 (engineer report, opus)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c`, branch `srvm-phase6c`, HEAD dc545aaa. **Not committed.**\n\nOnly two test files changed:\n- `layout_test.cljc` (+~200 / -~90)\n- `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (+~70 / -~45)\n\n`git diff --quiet -- src docs` is clean. I found no production defect.\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutant was applied by `collab/1792390000000-engineer-6c-fix2.mutants.py`. The script copies the file to `/tmp` with `copy2`, applies one exact replacement, and runs the quick tier on layout-test, safepoint-harness-test and store-write-audit-test. It then restores the file and checks `diff -q` against the backup.\n\n- All six restores were `diff -q` identical.\n- `git diff --quiet` is clean for `layout.cljc`. The two test files carry this round's own edits.\n- The baseline for these three namespaces is 38 tests, 3738 assertions, 0 failures.\n\n| Item | Mutant | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| N1 | `closures-round-trip` uses `h/file-wide` instead of `h/scoped` | **killed**: 1 error, `:ambiguous-image` |\n| N1 | `kernel-space` reads `@code-index`, ignoring the scope | **killed**: 2 failures, 3 errors |\n| N2 | injectivity guard removed | **killed**: 2 failures (`law-4-controls`) |\n| N2 | law-4 descriptor guard removed | **killed**: 2 failures (`law-4-controls`) |\n| N3 | `row-procedure` checks the top level only | **killed**: 24 failures (`free-env-nested-values`) |\n| N4 | stack and register image functions swapped in `image-collision` | **killed**: 4 failures (`alpha-equivalent-segments`) |\n\n## N1: scoping\n\n**Structural guard (harness).**\n- `kernel-space` now **throws when `*projected*` is unbound**. A world that is not scoped can no longer read the file-wide index without anyone noticing.\n- The new `h/file-wide` binds `*projected*` to `code-index`. It is the only way to read the global index on purpose.\n- Its single user is `alpha-equivalent-segments`' contamination check.\n\n**Sites now scoped.**\n- In `layout_test`, the new helper `in-world` runs a world's construction and its lookups in one `h/scoped`. These sites use it or `h/scoped`:\n  - `register-rd-from-a`, both cases;\n  - `stack-slices-partition`, the rows and the multi-frame fixture;\n  - `env-reconstruction`, through `envs`, `lifted-waits` and row 21;\n  - `closures-round-trip`, per case;\n  - the lift side of `free-env-values`.\n- In the harness, the non-safepoint and tampered-live cases of `layout-refusals` (`lane-lift`, `register-judge`, `spare-register`).\n\n**Codex's reproduction is now part of the test.** `closures-round-trip` first projects an alpha-renamed copy of every `closure-programs` fixture (`x`/`y`/`f` → `other-*`) file-wide. It then passes. Its file-wide mutant throws `:ambiguous-image`.\n\n## N2: law-4 guards\n\nThe two guards are now refusals, not `is`, so that a control can observe them firing without a reported failure:\n- `injective` throws `{:law-4 :injective :names …}`;\n- `canonical-equality` throws `{:law-4 :descriptors …}`.\n\n`law-4-controls` replaces the hand-built descriptor map with two real fixtures:\n\n- **One-lane descriptor change.** `(bare 1)` holds an extra ring under `:control/extra`, on the register lane only. The roots stay equal, so the root comparison cannot see it, and only the descriptor guard does. The test asserts `:law-4 :descriptors`, and that the key is present only in the register lane's descriptors.\n- **Duplicate correspondence.** On the stack lane, the world's new `:served` key (`lane-root` now honours it) twins every served table entry: two identities, one handle, so one logical name. The test asserts `:law-4 :injective` and that the name map is not injective.\n\n## N3: nested free-env values\n\nNew test: `layout-test/free-env-nested-values`. It covers 2 nestings × 4 values × 2 lanes × 2 directions.\n- **Nestings:** box `[1 [x]]` (path `[:free-env box 1 0]`) and box `{:nested x}` (path `[:free-env box 1]`).\n- **Closure and continuation.**\n  - Lowering into a native receiver refuses `:unsupported :free-env-value` with the exact path and 0 attaches.\n  - A native source refuses `:non-portable :free-env-value` with key `box` and 0 serves.\n  - The reference lane answers `\"B\"`.\n  - The continuation is captured inside `(fn [box] …)` as a tail call. That way its E differs from the free environment only on the lexical `box`, so the carrier itself lifts it.\n  - A continuation captured with any non-lexical E is refused earlier by the carrier, as `:inconsistent-state :free-env-mismatch`.\n- **Admitted controls.**\n  - **Primitive:** the program reads it back through `first`/`get`.\n  - **Authentic cursor reference:** minted by `engine/handle-cursor` on the source lane; the program's read goes through that nested cursor.\n  - Both cross in both directions through `h/crossed`, with attaches equal to the carried stream identities, and answer the reference value.\n\n## N4: receiver image\n\n`alpha-equivalent-segments` now asserts that the lower refusal's `:yin.k/image` is exactly `receiver-image` of each closure vector:\n- `dcode/image-hash` of `(:image (derive/stack-image v))` for `:stack`;\n- `rcode/register-hash` of `(derive/register-image v)` for `:register`.\n\nThe new case \"one of the pair carried, the other only projected: no collision\" (`alpha-world :one`) lowers into each native lane with 1 stream identity and 1 attach, and continues to `\"B\"`.\n\n## Verification (JVM, foreground)\n\n- **Quick tier**, `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the four requested namespaces: **67 tests, 4191 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n- **Slow tier**, `-i :slow`: **4 tests, 2724 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n  - This is down from 3517 assertions. The 793 that went away are exactly the former `is` guards: 4 injectivity checks and 1 descriptor check per lane-root, over 61 cases × 3 lanes and 61 cases. Those checks now run as refusals.\n- **Kondo** (`clj -M:kondo --lint` on both files): 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- **cljstyle fix** applied to both files.\n\n## Observation (not a 6c defect, not changed)\n\nOn every lane, including the reference lane, a primitive extracted from a guest collection and then applied fails with \"Cannot apply non-function\" (`:kind :map`). A primitive held at the top level of the free environment applies normally. The admitted-primitive control therefore returns the primitive instead of calling it. This is VM semantics outside this slice.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":165109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1571a1be-fcf5-41b6-a2c4-f2a5582b2e60","uuid":"ec49519e-7ec4-491f-9efe-1071d3b4dfdc","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:17:45.229Z","request_id":"req_011CfxxcQ1ZQbrogrf9T5fwV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016EKPM4urV31XfrdJBNv8vY":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/collab/1792390000000-engineer-6c-fix2.report.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 +07\n# Slice 6c fix round 2 (engineer report, opus)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c`, branch `srvm-phase6c`, HEAD dc545aaa. **Not committed.**\n\nOnly two test files changed:\n- `layout_test.cljc` (+~200 / -~90)\n- `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (+~70 / -~45)\n\n`git diff --quiet -- src docs` is clean. I found no production defect.\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutant was applied by `collab/1792390000000-engineer-6c-fix2.mutants.py`. The script copies the file to `/tmp` with `copy2`, applies one exact replacement, and runs the quick tier on layout-test, safepoint-harness-test and store-write-audit-test. It then restores the file and checks `diff -q` against the backup.\n\n- All six restores were `diff -q` identical.\n- `git diff --quiet` is clean for `layout.cljc`. The two test files carry this round's own edits.\n- The baseline for these three namespaces is 38 tests, 3738 assertions, 0 failures.\n\n| Item | Mutant | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| N1 | `closures-round-trip` uses `h/file-wide` instead of `h/scoped` | **killed**: 1 error, `:ambiguous-image` |\n| N1 | `kernel-space` reads `@code-index`, ignoring the scope | **killed**: 2 failures, 3 errors |\n| N2 | injectivity guard removed | **killed**: 2 failures (`law-4-controls`) |\n| N2 | law-4 descriptor guard removed | **killed**: 2 failures (`law-4-controls`) |\n| N3 | `row-procedure` checks the top level only | **killed**: 24 failures (`free-env-nested-values`) |\n| N4 | stack and register image functions swapped in `image-collision` | **killed**: 4 failures (`alpha-equivalent-segments`) |\n\n## N1: scoping\n\n**Structural guard (harness).**\n- `kernel-space` now **throws when `*projected*` is unbound**. A world that is not scoped can no longer read the file-wide index without anyone noticing.\n- The new `h/file-wide` binds `*projected*` to `code-index`. It is the only way to read the global index on purpose.\n- Its single user is `alpha-equivalent-segments`' contamination check.\n\n**Sites now scoped.**\n- In `layout_test`, the new helper `in-world` runs a world's construction and its lookups in one `h/scoped`. These sites use it or `h/scoped`:\n  - `register-rd-from-a`, both cases;\n  - `stack-slices-partition`, the rows and the multi-frame fixture;\n  - `env-reconstruction`, through `envs`, `lifted-waits` and row 21;\n  - `closures-round-trip`, per case;\n  - the lift side of `free-env-values`.\n- In the harness, the non-safepoint and tampered-live cases of `layout-refusals` (`lane-lift`, `register-judge`, `spare-register`).\n\n**Codex's reproduction is now part of the test.** `closures-round-trip` first projects an alpha-renamed copy of every `closure-programs` fixture (`x`/`y`/`f` → `other-*`) file-wide. It then passes. Its file-wide mutant throws `:ambiguous-image`.\n\n## N2: law-4 guards\n\nThe two guards are now refusals, not `is`, so that a control can observe them firing without a reported failure:\n- `injective` throws `{:law-4 :injective :names …}`;\n- `canonical-equality` throws `{:law-4 :descriptors …}`.\n\n`law-4-controls` replaces the hand-built descriptor map with two real fixtures:\n\n- **One-lane descriptor change.** `(bare 1)` holds an extra ring under `:control/extra`, on the register lane only. The roots stay equal, so the root comparison cannot see it, and only the descriptor guard does. The test asserts `:law-4 :descriptors`, and that the key is present only in the register lane's descriptors.\n- **Duplicate correspondence.** On the stack lane, the world's new `:served` key (`lane-root` now honours it) twins every served table entry: two identities, one handle, so one logical name. The test asserts `:law-4 :injective` and that the name map is not injective.\n\n## N3: nested free-env values\n\nNew test: `layout-test/free-env-nested-values`. It covers 2 nestings × 4 values × 2 lanes × 2 directions.\n- **Nestings:** box `[1 [x]]` (path `[:free-env box 1 0]`) and box `{:nested x}` (path `[:free-env box 1]`).\n- **Closure and continuation.**\n  - Lowering into a native receiver refuses `:unsupported :free-env-value` with the exact path and 0 attaches.\n  - A native source refuses `:non-portable :free-env-value` with key `box` and 0 serves.\n  - The reference lane answers `\"B\"`.\n  - The continuation is captured inside `(fn [box] …)` as a tail call. That way its E differs from the free environment only on the lexical `box`, so the carrier itself lifts it.\n  - A continuation captured with any non-lexical E is refused earlier by the carrier, as `:inconsistent-state :free-env-mismatch`.\n- **Admitted controls.**\n  - **Primitive:** the program reads it back through `first`/`get`.\n  - **Authentic cursor reference:** minted by `engine/handle-cursor` on the source lane; the program's read goes through that nested cursor.\n  - Both cross in both directions through `h/crossed`, with attaches equal to the carried stream identities, and answer the reference value.\n\n## N4: receiver image\n\n`alpha-equivalent-segments` now asserts that the lower refusal's `:yin.k/image` is exactly `receiver-image` of each closure vector:\n- `dcode/image-hash` of `(:image (derive/stack-image v))` for `:stack`;\n- `rcode/register-hash` of `(derive/register-image v)` for `:register`.\n\nThe new case \"one of the pair carried, the other only projected: no collision\" (`alpha-world :one`) lowers into each native lane with 1 stream identity and 1 attach, and continues to `\"B\"`.\n\n## Verification (JVM, foreground)\n\n- **Quick tier**, `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the four requested namespaces: **67 tests, 4191 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n- **Slow tier**, `-i :slow`: **4 tests, 2724 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n  - This is down from 3517 assertions. The 793 that went away are exactly the former `is` guards: 4 injectivity checks and 1 descriptor check per lane-root, over 61 cases × 3 lanes and 61 cases. Those checks now run as refusals.\n- **Kondo** (`clj -M:kondo --lint` on both files): 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- **cljstyle fix** applied to both files.\n\n## Observation (not a 6c defect, not changed)\n\nOn every lane, including the reference lane, a primitive extracted from a guest collection and then applied fails with \"Cannot apply non-function\" (`:kind :map`). A primitive held at the top level of the free environment applies normally. The admitted-primitive control therefore returns the primitive instead of calling it. This is VM semantics outside this slice.\n"}}}
